Read the file `prompt` in this directory — it is the complete brief for what I
want you to build. Follow it closely.

Summary of what it asks for: a frontend-only Persian (RTL) bakery website UI,
minimal editorial style, illustration-led rather than photography-led. No
backend, no CMS, no database, no auth, no APIs. It is a visual prototype I will
screenshot and show to a client.

Before you start writing code, tell me your plan for:

1. The type scale and spacing system — with no photography carrying the page,
   this is what the design lives or dies on
2. The palette (ivory background, espresso text, one muted accent — pick one and
   say which)
3. The component and file structure

Then build it.

Important notes:

- Hand-author the line illustrations as inline SVG React components in
  `src/components/illustrations/` — do not use an AI image generator and do not
  download stock assets. Keep one uniform stroke weight across the whole set;
  that consistency matters more than any single drawing. Use `currentColor` so
  they inherit the palette.
- Build the hero illustration and one category icon FIRST and show me those
  before drawing the rest, so we lock the style before it gets replicated 19
  times.
- The brand name and prices in the brief are invented. Use sensible Persian
  placeholders; I will replace them before the client sees this.
- When something is not working visually, remove it rather than adding more.
  Empty, well-composed whitespace beats a weak illustration.

When you are done, run `pnpm build` and `pnpm lint`, then start the dev server
and tell me the URL so I can look at it.

If you have Playwright MCP available, take screenshots at 375px and 1280px, look
at them, and iterate on spacing and typography before telling me it is finished.
If you do not have it, say so plainly instead of claiming you checked the
visuals.
